// PASSWORDSPRAY-ALWAYSONLINUX-T1110.003
//
// DETECTION QUERY (deployed rule SOC-BUILD-PASSWORDSPRAY-ALWAYSONLINUX-T1110.003)
// Recovered 2026-09-25 and reproduced verbatim below.
// Version reference: not recorded at build time.
// Rule settings supply the window: runs every 1 hour over the previous 1 hour.
//
// Observations from the v3 conformance review:
//   - Counts failed logons only, per host (by DeviceName). Fires at 8 or more
//     distinct accounts.
//   - No time filter in the query itself; it relies on the rule's 1-hour lookback.
//     Run ad hoc, it covers whatever time range is selected.
//   - TopSource is SourceList[0]. make_set() does not guarantee order, so this
//     is an arbitrary source, not the most frequent one. The IP entity maps to it.
//   - AccountList and SourceList are capped at 20 entries each. The 2026-07-19
//     case tried 38 accounts, so its account list would have been truncated.
//   - No exclusion for private or in-VNet sources, so the in-VNet Tenable scanner's
//     failures count toward the threshold. The playbook handles this at triage.
//   - AccountName is not checked for empty values; an empty name counts as one
//     distinct account.

DeviceLogonEvents
| where ActionType == "LogonFailed"
| where DeviceName startswith "linux-target-1"
| summarize
    Attempts=count(),
    Accounts=dcount(AccountName),
    Sources=dcount(RemoteIP),
    AccountList=make_set(AccountName, 20),
    SourceList=make_set(RemoteIP, 20),
    TimeGenerated=max(TimeGenerated)
  by DeviceName
| where Accounts >= 8
| extend TopSource = tostring(SourceList[0])
| extend ShortHost = tostring(split(DeviceName, ".")[0]);

// VERIFICATION QUERIES, v1 (HISTORICAL)
// From playbook v1, Block 5. Both were run 2026-07-12 over a seven-day window.
// Known defects (corrected in playbook v2, which scopes both queries to the
// case host and time window):
//   - Neither query filters on the affected host; both aggregate by RemoteIP
//     across every host, so unrelated hosts and accounts can combine.
//   - Query B does not check that a success came after the attempts.

// Query A (v1): spray shape and attempts-per-account ratio, all hosts.
// Observed 2026-07-12: 142 external attacking IPs across seven days.
DeviceLogonEvents
| where Timestamp > ago(7d)
| where ActionType == "LogonFailed"
| where not(ipv4_is_private(RemoteIP)) and isnotempty(RemoteIP)
| summarize FailedAttempts = count(), AccountsTried = dcount(AccountName),
            FirstSeen = min(Timestamp), LastSeen = max(Timestamp) by RemoteIP
| where FailedAttempts > 20
| extend AttemptsPerAccount = round(FailedAttempts * 1.0 / AccountsTried, 1)
| sort by FailedAttempts desc;

// Query B (v1): external sources with at least one successful logon, all hosts.
// Observed 2026-07-12: 64 external IPs with at least one success.
// It filters on Successes > 0 with no requirement for preceding failures, so it
// CAN return successes without failures. It cannot establish how credentials
// were obtained, that a success was malicious, or that it followed the attempts.
DeviceLogonEvents
| where Timestamp > ago(7d)
| summarize Failures  = countif(ActionType == "LogonFailed"),
            Successes = countif(ActionType == "LogonSuccess"),
            Accounts  = dcount(AccountName) by RemoteIP
| where not(ipv4_is_private(RemoteIP)) and isnotempty(RemoteIP)
| where Successes > 0
| sort by Failures desc

// VERIFICATION QUERIES, v2 (DRAFT, NOT YET RUN)
// See PB-PASSWORDSPRAY-ALWAYSONLINUX-T1110.003-v2.md, Block 5.
